  "id": "COMPOUND:24166 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Amphicoside appears to interact with DNA polymerase iota through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are involved in signaling and metabolic pathways. The evidence suggests that Amphicoside acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Lychnostatin 1, 14-Deoxy-11,12-dehydroandrographolide, and 1,2,3,5-Tetrahydroxyxanthone, which in turn target DNA polymerase iota. This indicates a potential mechanism where Amphicoside may modulate the activity of these compounds, which then exert their effects on DNA polymerase iota. The shared involvement of these targets in signaling pathways suggests a possible role for Amphicoside in regulating DNA polymerase iota activity, possibly through indirect interactions. The consistent scores across the three paths support a robust relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
